 a dart:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNand so terrible was the sight, that Moses said, I exceedingly fear and quake:)¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book9§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†but ye are come unto mount Sion, and unto the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to an innumerable company of angels,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›to the general assembly and church of the firstborn, which are written in heaven, and to God the Judge of all, and to the spirits of just men made perfect,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}and to Jesus the mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling, that speaketh better things than that of Abel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book9§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹See that ye refuse not him that speaketh. For if they escaped not who refused him that spake on earth, much more shall not we escape, if we turn away from him that speaketh from heaven:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~whose voice then shook the earth: but now he hath promised, saying, Yet once more I shake not the earth only, but also heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And this word, Yet once more, signifieth the removing of those things that are shaken, as of things that are made, that those things which cannot be shaken may remain.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book9§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWherefore we receiving a kingdom which cannot be moved, let us have grace, whereby we may serve God acceptably with reverence and godly fear:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ for our God is a consuming fire.¦layout ªlast_verse